Since which android-studio points to /snap/bin/android-studio, you installed it via Snap and can launch it directly by typing android-studio.

Launch Commands

• Run in the background. Type the command with an & so your terminal prompt stays free for other commands like adb:bash
android-studio &
Use code with caution.
• Detach completely (optional). If you want Android Studio to stay open even if you close this terminal window later, run:bash
nohup android-studio >/dev/null 2>&1 &
Use code with caution.

Next Steps for Your APK

• Start your virtual device. Once Android Studio opens, go to More Actions > Virtual Device Manager (or click the Device Manager icon on the right sidebar) and click the Play button next to your emulator.
• Install the APK. Once the emulator finishes booting up to the home screen, navigate back to ~/bidget/ubuntubitget in your terminal and run adb install "Bitget Wallet.apk".
Once the emulator is running, let me know if adb install "Bitget Wallet.apk" succeeds or if you hit an architecture (ABIS) or proxy error.
